  "reason": "The existing evidence shows that config_039 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) achieves the highest accuracy so far (0.725). This experiment tests whether replacing scvi_n200 with scgpt (a more advanced RNA encoder) in the same setup could further improve performance. It directly compares encoder choices while keeping other critical parameters (multiprofile, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion) consistent, isolating the impact of the RNA encoder. This is the best use of the final experiment to either confirm or refute the potential of scgpt in this context."
